- Device/session authentication, expiry, revocation, malformed Ed25519 keys and replay protection.
- Default-deny policy and no public adapter dispatcher bypass.
- Task-scoped single-use approvals and cross-device permission checks.
- AI planner schema validation and rejection of prohibited/injected operations.
- Outcome truthfulness for partial/interrupted execution and audit-persistence failure.
- Hash-chained audit integrity, redaction, tamper/truncation detection, and fail-closed recovery.
- Live HTTP lifecycle and persistent revocation recovery.
- Voice privacy defaults, push-to-talk, mute, cancellation, and transcript disposal (automated/simulated as applicable).
- HUD route/assets and browser keyboard/reduced-motion/error smoke checks.

## Required real-runtime acceptance

### Windows commands / Notepad
Run the backend on the actual Windows host and issue the command through the real JARVIS UI/text/voice path. Record the request, policy and approval decision, adapter invocation, OS process evidence, visible-window observation, audit entry, and user-facing result. Test denial, expired session, missing approval, spawn error, cancellation, timeout, and restart. Distinguish requested, awaiting approval, denied, failed, started, and verified. A mock or PID alone is not proof that a visible window is ready.

### Voice/audio
Test permission granted/denied, missing/disconnected microphone, explicit start/stop, mute, cancel, late/empty transcript, timeout, duplicate activation, page/session close, actual recognition engine and its local/remote data behavior, real TTS playback, unavailable voice, autoplay restriction, and stop/cancel. Confirm no capture at startup, wake word disabled by default, visible listening indicator, and no false speaking/listening status.

### Android / two phones
Build/install on physical devices. Verify enrollment proof-of-possession, TLS trust, signed requests, replay protection, independent identities/sessions/permissions, revocation, reconnect, notifications, approval expiry, and critical-action step-up. Revoke one phone and prove the other remains independent.

